f"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Calhoun County came in under 90% of normal in October to November 41 times in 75 years, more than any other pair. October to November is also the driest pair at 5.55 inches of normal. In 2025 on the middle, January to February and November to December each came in at 50% of normal. In 2026 so far, March to April sits at 23% of normal on the middle, and every grid had its driest year in 1954.</p>"}
